# Agent request kinds, the `open_run` and `refresh_ui` tools, and the web host for them (KAN-91 #1, #3)

## What to build

graph-manager's agent-request queue (`apps/graph-manager/src/server/agent-requests.ts`) holds UI requests that agent tools queue and the browser acts on. Today it has one kind, `start-run` (the `open_start_run` tool). This slice:

1. Turns `AgentRequest` into a **discriminated union on `kind`** with all five kinds the feature needs: `start-run`, `open-run`, `open-graph`, `propose-graph`, `refresh` (exact type below). `open-graph` and `propose-graph` are only typed here; their tools and web handling come later and must not be built in this slice.
2. Changes `AgentRequests.add` so a request replaces a pending one of the same terminal **only when it has the same kind**; `refresh` requests have no terminal, never replace anything, expire after 10 s (`REFRESH_TTL_MS`) and cannot be acked. Adds `get(id)`.
3. Adds two tools: `open_run { runId }` (queues `{ kind: "open-run", runId }`) and `refresh_ui {}` (queues `{ kind: "refresh" }`).
4. Web: `web/types.ts` gets the same union; `AgentRequestHost` (`web/agentRequests.tsx`) handles `open-run` (opens the run in the next free pane when the Terminals page shows the calling terminal, else toasts `<Agent> in <repo>: run <id>` with **Open** → `/runs/:ws/:runId`) and `refresh` (bumps a refresh counter in the overview provider; the overview poll re-polls now, and the page data hooks re-fetch).

Spec: `docs/prd/agent-supervisor.md` (sections "Tools (KAN-91)" rows `open_run` and `refresh_ui`, "Agent requests and the web", and Decisions rows "UI tools …", "`open_run`: …", "`refresh_ui` …").

Already in the codebase from earlier slices: `apps/graph-manager/src/server/tools/run-helpers.ts` exports
```ts
export function requireWorkspace(tc: ToolContext): Workspace | ToolResult;        // error text "this terminal is not inside a graph-manager workspace"
export async function runDirOrError(ws: Workspace, runId: string): Promise<string | ToolResult>; // error "unknown run <id>" for a bad id or missing run folder
export function isToolResult(x: unknown): x is ToolResult;
```
and `tools/index.ts` already lists more tools (`list_runs`, `get_run_log`, `list_graphs`, `get_node_output`, `get_artifacts`, `cancel_run`, `resume_run`). Read `run-helpers.ts` first and use it exactly as it is (if a signature differs slightly from the above, follow the file).

